---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj04.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The Old Practice — Directors' Bonus as an Appropriation of Retained Earnings" },
        { id: "s4", label: "THE KEY REFORM — Recognition as an Expense in the Period of Service" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Recognition Timing — Accrual Before Shareholders' Meeting Approval" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Presentation in the Statement of Income" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Accruing a Directors' Bonus Before Approval" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Contrasting Old vs New Treatment" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Compensation for service rendered is an expense, not a distribution of profit</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 4 addresses a GENUINELY significant reform in Japanese accounting practice: HOW should a company's payment of a BONUS to its DIRECTORS (役員賞与) be characterised? Under LONG-STANDING Japanese practice (rooted in the old Commercial Code), director bonuses were traditionally treated as an "APPROPRIATION OF RETAINED EARNINGS" — a DISTRIBUTION of profit, decided by the shareholders' general meeting ALONGSIDE dividends — rather than as compensation EXPENSE. This Statement ESTABLISHED that directors' bonuses must instead be recognised as an <strong>EXPENSE</strong>, in the period the related SERVICES were rendered — a fundamental, PRINCIPLE-DRIVEN change.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies paying bonuses to directors, executive officers, and similar officers</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies that pay BONUSES to DIRECTORS (取締役), AUDITORS/company auditors (監査役), and EXECUTIVE OFFICERS (執行役) — governing the RECOGNITION timing and classification of such payments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Old Practice — Directors' Bonus as an Appropriation of Retained Earnings</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Treated like a dividend, not a cost of doing business</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Under the OLD Commercial Code-era practice, a director's bonus was CONCEPTUALLY treated much like a DIVIDEND — a DISTRIBUTION of the company's ALREADY-EARNED profit, requiring approval at the shareholders' GENERAL MEETING (株主総会) ALONGSIDE the dividend resolution — appearing as an APPROPRIATION of Retained Earnings (利益剰余金の処分) rather than as an EXPENSE reducing the period's reported profit. This meant a company's REPORTED profit for the year did NOT reflect the ECONOMIC cost of director compensation actually EARNED during that year.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE KEY REFORM — Recognition as an Expense in the Period of Service</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Director compensation for services rendered is genuinely a cost of the business</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">ASBJ Statement No. 4 ESTABLISHED that a directors' bonus RELATING to services rendered DURING a given fiscal year must be recognised as an <strong>EXPENSE</strong> in the STATEMENT OF INCOME (損益計算書) FOR THAT YEAR — REGARDLESS of whether the SPECIFIC amount has yet been FORMALLY approved by the shareholders' general meeting. This reflects the PRINCIPLE that compensation for services ALREADY rendered represents a genuine ECONOMIC COST of the period, NOT a discretionary distribution of ALREADY-earned profit decided AFTER the fact — a MEANINGFUL conceptual and practical shift bringing Japanese practice CLOSER to how employee and management compensation is treated INTERNATIONALLY.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Recognition Timing — Accrual Before Shareholders' Meeting Approval</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A liability accrued for the estimated amount, ahead of formal approval</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Where a director's bonus RELATES to services rendered during the fiscal year, but has NOT yet been formally APPROVED by the shareholders' general meeting as of the balance sheet date, the company ACCRUES a LIABILITY for the ESTIMATED amount expected to be approved — recognising the related EXPENSE in the SAME period the services were rendered, rather than DEFERRING recognition until the LATER approval date.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Presentation in the Statement of Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Presented as an operating expense, reducing reported profit</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Directors' bonus expense is presented WITHIN the Statement of Income as an ORDINARY operating (or, depending on classification, a selling, general and administrative) EXPENSE — REDUCING the company's reported OPERATING and NET profit for the period, in CONTRAST to the OLD practice where it never touched the Statement of Income at all, appearing SOLELY as a post-profit APPROPRIATION.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Accruing a Directors' Bonus Before Approval</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising the expense ahead of the shareholders' meeting</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A fiscal year-end bonus accrual</div><div class="wk-body">A company's fiscal year ends March 31. Directors have rendered services throughout the year, and management estimates the board will propose (and the shareholders' meeting in June will likely approve) a total directors' bonus of ¥80,000,000 relating to the fiscal year just ended.</div><div class="wk-answer">At March 31 (the fiscal year end), the company recognises an <strong>¥80,000,000 EXPENSE</strong> in the Statement of Income for the year, with a corresponding ACCRUED LIABILITY on the Balance Sheet — even though the shareholders' meeting FORMALLY approving the specific amount doesn't occur until JUNE, several months LATER.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Contrasting Old vs New Treatment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The same ¥80,000,000, two very different presentations</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: The same bonus, before and after the reform</div><div class="wk-body">Using the same ¥80,000,000 directors' bonus from the prior example.</div><div class="wk-answer"><strong>Under the OLD practice:</strong> the ¥80,000,000 would NOT appear in the Statement of Income at all — it would be presented SOLELY as an APPROPRIATION of Retained Earnings, AFTER net profit is already determined, leaving REPORTED profit UNAFFECTED.<br><strong>Under ASBJ Statement No. 4:</strong> the SAME ¥80,000,000 REDUCES reported operating and net profit DIRECTLY, as a genuine EXPENSE of the period — a MATERIAL difference in REPORTED profitability for companies with SIGNIFICANT director bonus arrangements.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 4 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>The amount of directors' bonus expense recognised for the period</span><span>The basis of the accrual estimate where the shareholders' meeting has not yet formally approved the amount</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a bonus genuinely relates to services rendered in the current period, warranting accrual</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>The estimated bonus amount expected to be approved at the forthcoming shareholders' general meeting</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 4)</span><span>IFRS (IAS 19)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Director/employee bonus classification</span><span>EXPENSE, recognised as services are rendered</span><span>EXPENSE, recognised as services are rendered (short-term employee benefits) — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Historical alternative (profit appropriation)</span><span>Formerly permitted, NOW abandoned</span><span>NEVER a recognised alternative under IFRS — compensation is always an expense</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This reform brought J-GAAP INTO ALIGNMENT with the internationally UNIVERSAL principle that compensation for services rendered is an EXPENSE — the OLD Japanese practice of treating director bonuses as a profit APPROPRIATION was a genuinely DISTINCTIVE, LOCAL departure that this Statement CORRECTED, moving J-GAAP CLOSER to IFRS/IAS 19 on this specific point.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every directors' bonus event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Directors' bonus accrual</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Expensed in the period services are rendered, with a corresponding accrued liability</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 6</span><span>Statement of Changes in Net Assets — reflects the presentation shift away from the old profit appropriation approach</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 8</span><span>Share-based Payment — governs a related, but distinct, form of director/employee compensation</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Directors' bonus (役員賞与)</div><div class="glossary-def">A bonus paid to directors, auditors, or executive officers, recognised as an expense in the period services are rendered under ASBJ Statement No. 4.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Appropriation of Retained Earnings (利益剰余金の処分)</div><div class="glossary-def">The former practice of treating director bonuses as a post-profit distribution decided by the shareholders' general meeting, rather than an expense — now abandoned.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
